            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-5278",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "coreutils: Heap Buffer Under-Read in GNU Coreutils sort via Key Specification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-5278\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: coreutils\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-5278](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278)\nA flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
