            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-6297",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "It was discovered that dpkg-deb does not properly sanitize directory p ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "It was discovered that dpkg-deb does not properly sanitize directory permissions when extracting a control member into a temporary directory, which is\ndocumented as being a safe operation even on untrusted data. This may result in leaving temporary files behind on cleanup. Given automated and repeated execution of dpkg-deb commands on\nadversarial .deb packages or with well compressible files, placed\ninside a directory with permissions not allowing removal by a non-root\nuser, this can end up in a DoS scenario due to causing disk quota\nexhaustion or disk full conditions."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-6297\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: dpkg\nFixed Version: 1.21.23\nLink: [CVE-2025-6297](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-6297)\nIt was discovered that dpkg-deb does not properly sanitize directory permissions when extracting a control member into a temporary directory, which is\ndocumented as being a safe operation even on untrusted data. This may result in leaving temporary files behind on cleanup. Given automated and repeated execution of dpkg-deb commands on\nadversarial .deb packages or with well compressible files, placed\ninside a directory with permissions not allowing removal by a non-root\nuser, this can end up in a DoS scenario due to causing disk quota\nexhaustion or disk full conditions."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-6297",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-27943",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
