              "id": "CVE-2026-57062",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "GnuPG: Incorrect cryptographic message parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "CMS (Cryptographic Message Syntax) parsing in gpgsm in GnuPG through 2.5.20 mishandles the CMS format for AES-GCM because aes-ICVlen is supposed to be 12 bytes but 4 bytes is accepted. NOTE: this is related to CVE-2026-34182."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-57062\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: gpgv\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-57062](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-57062)\nCMS (Cryptographic Message Syntax) parsing in gpgsm in GnuPG through 2.5.20 mishandles the CMS format for AES-GCM because aes-ICVlen is supposed to be 12 bytes but 4 bytes is accepted. NOTE: this is related to CVE-2026-34182."
              },
