            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4802",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: static setuid binary dlopen may incorrectly search LD_LIBRARY_PATH"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Untrusted LD_LIBRARY_PATH environment variable vulnerability in the GNU C Library version 2.27 to 2.38 allows attacker controlled loading of dynamically shared library in statically compiled setuid binaries that call dlopen (including internal dlopen calls after setlocale or calls to NSS functions such as getaddrinfo)."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-4802\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: 2.36-9+deb12u11\nLink: [CVE-2025-4802](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-4802)\nUntrusted LD_LIBRARY_PATH environment variable vulnerability in the GNU C Library version 2.27 to 2.38 allows attacker controlled loading of dynamically shared library in statically compiled setuid binaries that call dlopen (including internal dlopen calls after setlocale or calls to NSS functions such as getaddrinfo)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-4802",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-8058",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: Double free in glibc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The regcomp function in the GNU C library version from 2.4 to 2.41 is \nsubject to a double free if some previous allocation fails. It can be \naccomplished either by a malloc failure or by using an interposed malloc\n that injects random malloc failures. The double free can allow buffer \nmanipulation depending of how the regex is constructed. This issue \naffects all architectures and ABIs supported by the GNU C library."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-8058\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: 2.36-9+deb12u13\nLink: [CVE-2025-8058](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-8058)\nThe regcomp function in the GNU C library version from 2.4 to 2.41 is \nsubject to a double free if some previous allocation fails. It can be \naccomplished either by a malloc failure or by using an interposed malloc\n that injects random malloc failures. The double free can allow buffer \nmanipulation depending of how the regex is constructed. This issue \naffects all architectures and ABIs supported by the GNU C library."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-8058",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-0915",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: glibc: Information disclosure via zero-valued network query"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling getnetbyaddr or getnetbyaddr_r with a configured nsswitch.conf that specifies the library's DNS backend for networks and queries for a zero-valued network in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.42 can leak stack contents to the configured DNS resolver."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-0915\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: 2.36-9+deb12u14\nLink: [CVE-2026-0915](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-0915)\nCalling getnetbyaddr or getnetbyaddr_r with a configured nsswitch.conf that specifies the library's DNS backend for networks and queries for a zero-valued network in the GNU C Library version 2.0 to version 2.42 can leak stack contents to the configured DNS resolver."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-0915",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-4046",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: glibc: Denial of Service via iconv() function with specific character sets"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The iconv() function in the GNU C Library versions 2.43 and earlier may crash due to an assertion failure when converting inputs from the IBM1390 or IBM1399 character sets, which may be used to remotely crash an application.\n\n\n\nThis vulnerability can be trivially mitigated by removing the IBM1390 and IBM1399 character sets from systems that do not need them."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-4046\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: 2.36-9+deb12u14\nLink: [CVE-2026-4046](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4046)\nThe iconv() function in the GNU C Library versions 2.43 and earlier may crash due to an assertion failure when converting inputs from the IBM1390 or IBM1399 character sets, which may be used to remotely crash an application.\n\n\n\nThis vulnerability can be trivially mitigated by removing the IBM1390 and IBM1399 character sets from systems that do not need them."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4046",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-4437",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: glibc: Incorrect DNS response parsing via crafted DNS server response"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling gethostbyaddr or gethostbyaddr_r with a configured nsswitch.conf that specifies the library's DNS backend in the GNU C Library version 2.34 to version 2.43 could, with a crafted response from the configured DNS server, result in a violation of the DNS specification that causes the application to treat a non-answer section of the DNS response as a valid answer."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-4437\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: 2.36-9+deb12u14\nLink: [CVE-2026-4437](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4437)\nCalling gethostbyaddr or gethostbyaddr_r with a configured nsswitch.conf that specifies the library's DNS backend in the GNU C Library version 2.34 to version 2.43 could, with a crafted response from the configured DNS server, result in a violation of the DNS specification that causes the application to treat a non-answer section of the DNS response as a valid answer."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4437",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-5435",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: glibc: Out-of-bounds write via TSIG record processing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The deprecated functions ns_printrrf, ns_printrr and fp_nquery in the GNU C Library version 2.2 and newer fail to enforce the caller-supplied buffer length, and can result in an out-of-bounds write when printing TSIG records."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-5435\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libc6\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-5435](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5435)\nThe deprecated functions ns_printrrf, ns_printrr and fp_nquery in the GNU C Library version 2.2 and newer fail to enforce the caller-supplied buffer length, and can result in an out-of-bounds write when printing TSIG records."
