            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-4878",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libcap: libcap: Privilege escalation via TOCTOU race condition in cap_set_file()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libcap. A local unprivileged user can exploit a Time-of-check-to-time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition in the `cap_set_file()` function. This allows an attacker with write access to a parent directory to redirect file capability updates to an attacker-controlled file. By doing so, capabilities can be injected into or stripped from unintended executables, leading to privilege escalation."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-4878\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: libcap2\nFixed Version: 1:2.66-4+deb12u3\nLink: [CVE-2026-4878](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4878)\nA flaw was found in libcap. A local unprivileged user can exploit a Time-of-check-to-time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition in the `cap_set_file()` function. This allows an attacker with write access to a parent directory to redirect file capability updates to an attacker-controlled file. By doing so, capabilities can be injected into or stripped from unintended executables, leading to privilege escalation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4878",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-1390",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libcap: pam_cap: Fix potential configuration parsing error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The PAM module pam_cap.so of libcap configuration supports group names starting with “@”, during actual parsing, configurations not starting with “@” are incorrectly recognized as group names. This may result in nonintended users being granted an inherited capability set, potentially leading to security risks. Attackers can exploit this vulnerability to achieve local privilege escalation on systems where /etc/security/capability.conf is used to configure user inherited privileges by constructing specific usernames."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-1390\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libcap2\nFixed Version: 1:2.66-4+deb12u1\nLink: [CVE-2025-1390](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-1390)\nThe PAM module pam_cap.so of libcap configuration supports group names starting with “@”, during actual parsing, configurations not starting with “@” are incorrectly recognized as group names. This may result in nonintended users being granted an inherited capability set, potentially leading to security risks. Attackers can exploit this vulnerability to achieve local privilege escalation on systems where /etc/security/capability.conf is used to configure user inherited privileges by constructing specific usernames."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-1390",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
