              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-3576",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2018-5709",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "krb5: integer overflow in dbentry-\u003en_key_data in kadmin/dbutil/dump.c"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) through 1.16. There is a variable \"dbentry-\u003en_key_data\" in kadmin/dbutil/dump.c that can store 16-bit data but unknowingly the developer has assigned a \"u4\" variable to it, which is for 32-bit data. An attacker can use this vulnerability to affect other artifacts of the database as we know that a Kerberos database dump file contains trusted data."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2018-5709\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libkrb5support0\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2018-5709](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-5709)\nAn issue was discovered in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) through 1.16. There is a variable \"dbentry-\u003en_key_data\" in kadmin/dbutil/dump.c that can store 16-bit data but unknowingly the developer has assigned a \"u4\" variable to it, which is for 32-bit data. An attacker can use this vulnerability to affect other artifacts of the database as we know that a Kerberos database dump file contains trusted data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2018-5709",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
