            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11850",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "krb5: krb5: integer underflow in berval2tl_data() leads to heap out-of-bounds read"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An integer underflow vulnerability was found in MIT krb5 in the berval2tl_data() function in plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c. The function performs an unsigned subtraction (bv_len - 2) without a prior bounds check. When bv_len is 0 or 1, the subtraction wraps to a large value which is then truncated to uint16_t, yielding 0xFFFE (65534) or 0xFFFF (65535). The subsequent malloc succeeds and memcpy reads up to 65534 bytes from a 0-1 byte buffer, resulting in a heap out-of-bounds read.\nThe attack vector involves a malicious or compromised LDAP KDB backend returning a krbExtraData attribute with bv_len \u003c 2, triggering the underflow when the KDC or kadmind reads principal data."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11850\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libkrb5support0\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-11850](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11850)\nAn integer underflow vulnerability was found in MIT krb5 in the berval2tl_data() function in plugins/kdb/ldap/libkdb_ldap/ldap_principal2.c. The function performs an unsigned subtraction (bv_len - 2) without a prior bounds check. When bv_len is 0 or 1, the subtraction wraps to a large value which is then truncated to uint16_t, yielding 0xFFFE (65534) or 0xFFFF (65535). The subsequent malloc succeeds and memcpy reads up to 65534 bytes from a 0-1 byte buffer, resulting in a heap out-of-bounds read.\nThe attack vector involves a malicious or compromised LDAP KDB backend returning a krbExtraData attribute with bv_len \u003c 2, triggering the underflow when the KDC or kadmind reads principal data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11850",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-31115",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "xz: XZ has a heap-use-after-free bug in threaded .xz decoder"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XZ Utils provide a general-purpose data-compression library plus command-line tools. In XZ Utils 5.3.3alpha to 5.8.0, the multithreaded .xz decoder in liblzma has a bug where invalid input can at least result in a crash. The effects include heap use after free and writing to an address based on the null pointer plus an offset. Applications and libraries that use the lzma_stream_decoder_mt function are affected. The bug has been fixed in XZ Utils 5.8.1, and the fix has been committed to the v5.4, v5.6, v5.8, and master branches in the xz Git repository. No new release packages will be made from the old stable branches, but a standalone patch is available that applies to all affected releases."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-31115\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: liblzma5\nFixed Version: 5.4.1-1\nLink: [CVE-2025-31115](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-31115)\nXZ Utils provide a general-purpose data-compression library plus command-line tools. In XZ Utils 5.3.3alpha to 5.8.0, the multithreaded .xz decoder in liblzma has a bug where invalid input can at least result in a crash. The effects include heap use after free and writing to an address based on the null pointer plus an offset. Applications and libraries that use the lzma_stream_decoder_mt function are affected. The bug has been fixed in XZ Utils 5.8.1, and the fix has been committed to the v5.4, v5.6, v5.8, and master branches in the xz Git repository. No new release packages will be made from the old stable branches, but a standalone patch is available that applies to all affected releases."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-31115",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-34743",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "xz: XZ Utils: Denial of Service via buffer overflow in index decoding"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "XZ Utils provide a general-purpose data-compression library plus command-line tools. Prior to version 5.8.3, if lzma_index_decoder() was used to decode an Index that contained no Records, the resulting lzma_index was left in a state where where a subsequent lzma_index_append() would allocate too little memory, and a buffer overflow would occur. This issue has been patched in version 5.8.3."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-34743\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: liblzma5\nFixed Version: 5.4.1-1+deb12u1\nLink: [CVE-2026-34743](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34743)\nXZ Utils provide a general-purpose data-compression library plus command-line tools. Prior to version 5.8.3, if lzma_index_decoder() was used to decode an Index that contained no Records, the resulting lzma_index was left in a state where where a subsequent lzma_index_append() would allocate too little memory, and a buffer overflow would occur. This issue has been patched in version 5.8.3."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-34743",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
