            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13757",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "p11-kit: Stack exhaustion via unbounded recursion in RPC attribute parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in p11-kit. The RPC message attribute parsing functions p11_rpc_message_get_attribute() and p11_rpc_message_get_attribute_array_value() form a mutually-recursive call chain with no recursion depth limit when processing nested CKA_WRAP_TEMPLATE, CKA_UNWRAP_TEMPLATE, and CKA_DERIVE_TEMPLATE attributes. An unauthenticated attacker with local access to the p11-kit RPC Unix domain socket can send a specially crafted request with deeply nested template attributes, causing stack exhaustion and crashing the p11-kit server process and its dependent services."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13757\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libp11-kit0\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-13757](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-13757)\nA flaw was found in p11-kit. The RPC message attribute parsing functions p11_rpc_message_get_attribute() and p11_rpc_message_get_attribute_array_value() form a mutually-recursive call chain with no recursion depth limit when processing nested CKA_WRAP_TEMPLATE, CKA_UNWRAP_TEMPLATE, and CKA_DERIVE_TEMPLATE attributes. An unauthenticated attacker with local access to the p11-kit RPC Unix domain socket can send a specially crafted request with deeply nested template attributes, causing stack exhaustion and crashing the p11-kit server process and its dependent services."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-13757",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18938",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "p11-kit: Integer overflow in RPC attribute-array length calculation can under-allocate nested attribute storage on 32 bit systems"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in p11-kit. A local attacker, or one with equivalent access to a reachable RPC channel, could exploit an integer overflow vulnerability. By sending specially crafted messages, the attacker can cause the system to miscalculate memory allocation for nested attributes. This leads to a memory corruption issue, specifically a heap out-of-bounds write, which can crash the p11-kit RPC parsing process, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS). This vulnerability is only exploitable on 32 bit systems."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-18938\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libp11-kit0\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-18938](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-18938)\nA flaw was found in p11-kit. A local attacker, or one with equivalent access to a reachable RPC channel, could exploit an integer overflow vulnerability. By sending specially crafted messages, the attacker can cause the system to miscalculate memory allocation for nested attributes. This leads to a memory corruption issue, specifically a heap out-of-bounds write, which can crash the p11-kit RPC parsing process, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS). This vulnerability is only exploitable on 32 bit systems."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-18938",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-6020",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "linux-pam: Linux-pam directory Traversal"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in linux-pam. The module pam_namespace may use access user-controlled paths without proper protection, allowing local users to elevate their privileges to root via multiple symlink attacks and race conditions."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-6020\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: libpam0g\nFixed Version: 1.5.2-6+deb12u2\nLink: [CVE-2025-6020](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-6020)\nA flaw was found in linux-pam. The module pam_namespace may use access user-controlled paths without proper protection, allowing local users to elevate their privileges to root via multiple symlink attacks and race conditions."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-6020",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-10041",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "pam: libpam: Libpam vulnerable to read hashed password"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in PAM. The secret information is stored in memory, where the attacker can trigger the victim program to execute by sending characters to its standard input (stdin). As this occurs, the attacker can train the branch predictor to execute an ROP chain speculatively. This flaw could result in leaked passwords, such as those found in /etc/shadow while performing authentications."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-10041\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libpam0g\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-10041](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-10041)\nA vulnerability was found in PAM. The secret information is stored in memory, where the attacker can trigger the victim program to execute by sending characters to its standard input (stdin). As this occurs, the attacker can train the branch predictor to execute an ROP chain speculatively. This flaw could result in leaked passwords, such as those found in /etc/shadow while performing authentications."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-10041",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-22365",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "pam: allowing unprivileged user to block another user namespace"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "linux-pam (aka Linux PAM) before 1.6.0 allows attackers to cause a denial of service (blocked login process) via mkfifo because the openat call (for protect_dir) lacks O_DIRECTORY."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-22365\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libpam0g\nFixed Version: 1.5.2-6+deb12u2\nLink: [CVE-2024-22365](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-22365)\nlinux-pam (aka Linux PAM) before 1.6.0 allows attackers to cause a denial of service (blocked login process) via mkfifo because the openat call (for protect_dir) lacks O_DIRECTORY."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-22365",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54411",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "linux-pam: Plaintext password recovery via timing discrepancy in pam_userdb module"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Linux-PAM through 1.7.2 contains an observable timing discrepancy (CWE-208) in the pam_userdb module's plaintext-password comparison path in modules/pam_userdb/pam_userdb.c that allows a local or network-adjacent attacker able to repeatedly drive authentication through a calling service to recover the plaintext password of a target account by measuring response-timing differences. The comparison uses strncmp() (or strncasecmp() when PAM_ICASE_ARG is set) preceded by a length-equality check, so the time to reject a candidate depends on the index of the first differing byte and on whether the candidate's length matches the stored password, leaking the password length and individual prefix bytes. The vulnerable path is reached when the administrator configures pam_userdb with crypt=none, with an unrecognized crypt method, or without a crypt= argument, causing the module to store and compare credentials in plaintext."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54411\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libpam0g\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-54411](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54411)\nLinux-PAM through 1.7.2 contains an observable timing discrepancy (CWE-208) in the pam_userdb module's plaintext-password comparison path in modules/pam_userdb/pam_userdb.c that allows a local or network-adjacent attacker able to repeatedly drive authentication through a calling service to recover the plaintext password of a target account by measuring response-timing differences. The comparison uses strncmp() (or strncasecmp() when PAM_ICASE_ARG is set) preceded by a length-equality check, so the time to reject a candidate depends on the index of the first differing byte and on whether the candidate's length matches the stored password, leaking the password length and individual prefix bytes. The vulnerable path is reached when the administrator configures pam_userdb with crypt=none, with an unrecognized crypt method, or without a crypt= argument, causing the module to store and compare credentials in plaintext."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54411",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-7458",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sqlite: SQLite integer overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An integer overflow in the sqlite3KeyInfoFromExprList function in SQLite versions 3.39.2 through 3.41.1 allows an attacker with the ability to execute arbitrary SQL statements to cause a denial of service or disclose sensitive information from process memory via a crafted SELECT statement with a large number of expressions in the ORDER BY clause."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-7458\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: libsqlite3-0\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-7458](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-7458)\nAn integer overflow in the sqlite3KeyInfoFromExprList function in SQLite versions 3.39.2 through 3.41.1 allows an attacker with the ability to execute arbitrary SQL statements to cause a denial of service or disclose sensitive information from process memory via a crafted SELECT statement with a large number of expressions in the ORDER BY clause."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-7458",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
