            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-12133",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libtasn1: Inefficient DER Decoding in libtasn1 Leading to Potential Remote DoS"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in libtasn1 causes inefficient handling of specific certificate data. When processing a large number of elements in a certificate, libtasn1 takes much longer than expected, which can slow down or even crash the system. This flaw allows an attacker to send a specially crafted certificate, causing a denial of service attack."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-12133\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libtasn1-6\nFixed Version: 4.19.0-2+deb12u1\nLink: [CVE-2024-12133](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12133)\nA flaw in libtasn1 causes inefficient handling of specific certificate data. When processing a large number of elements in a certificate, libtasn1 takes much longer than expected, which can slow down or even crash the system. This flaw allows an attacker to send a specially crafted certificate, causing a denial of service attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12133",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "scanner:Trivy"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-13151",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libtasn1: libtasn1: Denial of Service via stack-based buffer overflow in asn1_expend_octet_string"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
